title paint_paragraph_boxed -- the paragraph's vertical set, GREEN
prompt autonomous loop -- recur; next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Season G open-media
think The text-paint family carried horizontal set (paint_paragraph_aligned: left/centre/right within the content box) and a clip companion, yet no vertical placement -- the block always sat at its origin, with no way to centre it or flush it to the bottom of a panel taller than itself. The missing axis a real text region needs is exactly that: place the whole stack top, middle, or bottom within a box.
think Wrote paint_paragraph_boxed as pure composition -- wrap once to learn the line count, compute the block height (mirroring paint_paragraph_aligned's own box_bottom offset: (lines-1)*line_step + ch), refuse ParagraphBoxTooShort if the block is taller than the box (the strict all-or-nothing companion to the clipping painter), else offset the origin_y down by the vertical slack (top 0, bottom slack, middle slack/2) and DELEGATE the wrap-stack-paint to paint_paragraph_aligned unchanged. Single-stranded: the horizontal set, the disjoint bands, and the target box check all stay in one place; the new routine only decides where the block's top sits.
think Proved four ways against the plain paragraph as ground truth: a top set into a box six rows taller equals paint_paragraph at origin 0; middle equals it at slack/2; bottom equals it at the whole slack -- each byte-for-byte. Every vertical set changes exactly the same pixel count as the strict block (vertical placement moves the stack down as one, adding none, dropping none); bottom differs from top (the block truly moved); a box one row shorter than the block refuses ParagraphBoxTooShort by name, buffer untouched.
obs GREEN on the first build; tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, witness GREEN with four new grep gates. Rota this lap read item 15 (TAME_CORE, with TAME_GUIDANCE) -- fitting, since this lap wrote Rye: >=2 asserts per fn stated positively, u32 coordinates with u64 sums before the bound check, a named refusal at the edge, no new storage.
obs Single-stranded held: the boxed painter delegates to paint_paragraph_aligned rather than re-implementing the stack, so both share one geometry and one target check -- the belt-and-brace the aligned painter already keeps carries through the vertical set for free.
loom witness=text_paint_witness result=GREEN boxed_slack=6 boxed_block_h=15 para_pixels=79
